Migrate casing checks to the Rust side

Move SymbolNotCamelCase, SymbolNotSnakeCase, and VariableNotSnakeCase off
the eqlog-eqlog side into a new `casing` module. All three are pure AST
walks: decl names pick their casing from the symbol kind, and every
variable occurrence in a rule body must be snake_case. The pass runs
right after scope resolution and its errors are merged with the other
Rust and eqlog-side errors through `CompileError`'s `Ord`.
